                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued August 31 at 10:26PM MST until September 1 at 5:15AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Paria River in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 515 AM MST Tuesday.\n\n* At 1026 PM MST, a river gauge on the Paria River reported a rapid\nrise of about 4 feet from thunderstorms producing heavy rain over\nthe Paria River. Up to 2 inches of rain have fallen. Flash flooding\nis ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Paria River.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nParia River.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nParia Canyon, Paria River Slot Canyon and Vermilion Cliffs National\nMonument.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nParia River.",
                "instruction": "Get out of the Paria River slot canyon! Flood waters will flow down\nthe Paria River, reaching near the confluence with the Colorado River\nat Lees Ferry by 6 AM.",
